T*
(The project uses a full-stack split between a Next.js frontend and an Express + TypeScript) Tj
T*
(backend. The frontend owns the user experience, routing, filters, compare state, and form) Tj
T*
(interactions. The backend owns validation, database queries, authentication flow, saved) Tj
T*
(colleges, and response consistency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The backend is layered into controllers, routes, services, models, and utilities.) Tj
T*
(Controllers keep request/response logic thin, services contain database logic, and utilities) Tj
T*
(handle shared concerns such as validation, auth extraction, API responses, and database) Tj
T*
(connection setup.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
