T*
(Pagination uses LIMIT/OFFSET because it is simple and clear for an MVP. For much larger) Tj
T*
(datasets or deep pagination, cursor pagination would be more scalable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The compare system supports 2 to 3 colleges. This keeps the UX readable on desktop and) Tj
T*
(mobile. More colleges would create wide, hard-to-read tables and reduce decision clarity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The product uses a rule-based decision score rather than machine learning. This keeps) Tj
T*
(recommendations explainable and easy to debug. A later version could add personalized) Tj
T*
(ranking based on user preferences, saved behavior, and exam profile.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Some data fields are nullable, especially placement percentage and average package. The UI) Tj
T*
(displays "Data not available" instead of assuming zero or hiding the field. This avoids) Tj
T*
(misleading students.) Tj
