(What Was Optimized For) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
() Tj
T*
(The main optimization was clarity. The platform shows the few metrics students need first:) Tj
T*
(rating, fees, placement, average package, ranking, and available courses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The second optimization was speed. Listing pages use pagination, backend filters are) Tj
T*
(query-driven, filter options are fetched through metadata endpoints, and the frontend avoids) Tj
T*
(redundant hardcoded data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The third optimization was decision support. The app supports search, filtering, detail) Tj
T*
(view, compare, save, and login-backed shortlist flow. The compare page highlights stronger) Tj
T*
(values so users can make decisions faster.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The fourth optimization was maintainability. The codebase is split into reusable frontend) Tj
T*
(components and backend service layers, so new entities such as exams, reviews, rankings, and) Tj
T*
(predictors can be added without rewriting the entire app.) Tj
